From 86c934cdefbf2b3176834e5342371ec0b2e8c7e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:30:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 103/116] DXF: the SAB of the ACIS entities as SAT with all the
 precision

dwg_convert_SAB_to_SAT1 wrote the SAB of R2004+ drawings to DXF as SAT,
which was not readable: the doubles with %g (6 digits, the geometry
changed), the longs as pointers $n, the logicals of the curves and
surfaces as F instead of forward_v and I, the header strings broken into
pieces ("A utodesk A utoCA D"), the end marker cut, the version changed
to the one of the DWG with R2013+ content, the history attributes
dropped. And the SAB of AutoCAD's R2018 ("ASM BinaryFile4") not at all.
Use dwg_convert_SAB_to_SAT: the same version and records, the shortest
exact doubles, the words of the grammar, blocks of whole lines.

* src/out_dxf.c (dwg_convert_SAB_to_SAT1): Use dwg_convert_SAB_to_SAT.
(new_encr_sat_data_line, SAT_boolean): Remove.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
